This month, additional charges were incurred for door and ceiling repairs.

Regarding carpet cleaning, we included VAT in the price. This is because we agreed on $400 this year, but last year it was $300 + GST, so this time we included GST.This will reduce the cost burden somewhat.


Hello everyone! In this video, I'll be introducing a simulation of MicroMouse's maze-finding algorithm.

Although I have tried this many times in the past, in this final project, I used the inheritance function of object-oriented techniques to derive five similar objects from one object.


The cerebrum and cerebellum were designed to mimic the biological world, and the body was also implemented. The cerebrum was designed to primarily function as a way to think about finding a maze, while the cerebellum was designed to primarily function as a way of moving. The body was designed to represent motors as legs, encoders as arms, infrared sensors as eyes, controllers as the mind, and various report data outputs as the mouth.

The framework has also been configured to allow for standard implementation of these features. Let's enjoy!